From c0642c590f8a7a6b3a96bb2109f8b7929b40ad60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:03:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd, rdnsmapd, strongswan: audit 2026-10-06 - the VPN
 client key row needs a login, the name map reads LAN bridges only, strongSwan
 6.0.6 set

- httpd: the stock mime_handlers row that serves the WireGuard client
  configuration image (wgs_client.png) was reachable without a login, so
  anyone on the LAN could fetch a client's private key. The row now
  requires the session like every other config download.
- rdnsmapd: its AF_PACKET socket took DNS replies from every interface,
  including the WAN, so an off-path sender could plant names in the Flow
  Explorer map. Frames are now accepted only from a LAN bridge (br*).
- strongSwan: the 6.0.6 security fixes (RADIUS, EAP-SIM/AKA, PKCS#5,
  constraints, gmp RSA, PKCS#7, TLS server) carried onto the 6.0.x tree,
  with the upstream test change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
